Orange Pi Zero: describe XR819 Wi-Fi and optional audio and SPI devices.

Add the XR819 compatible and PG10 host-wake interrupt for the out-of-tree
xradio driver, following Armbian's device-tree patch.

Add audio routing, a userspace SPI1 device and stable SPI bus aliases.
Keep the audio codec and SPI1 disabled by default.

Use the downstream "allwinner,spi-dev" compatible for userspace SPI
access and add matching entries to the spidev driver. This follows
Armbian's approach without borrowing an unrelated chip's identity.
The compatible is a local convention, not an official Allwinner binding.

Armbian XR819 reference:
https://github.com/armbian/build/blob/main/patch/kernel/archive/sunxi-6.12/patches.armbian/arm-dts-sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero-fix-xradio-interrupt.patch

Armbian spidev reference:
https://github.com/armbian/build/blob/main/patch/kernel/archive/sunxi-6.12/patches.armbian/drv-spi-spidev-Add-armbian-spi-dev-compatible.patch

